# Every file in this repo is stored AND checked out with LF endings — no CR, on any platform.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides `core.autocrlf`, which is on by default on Windows and is what put CRLF in
# these blobs in the first place. That is not a cosmetic preference: `ops.rs` and `vocab.rs`
# GENERATE files here and then compare what they generated against what is on disk, so a working
# copy git handed back as CRLF failed the comparison on every Windows machine — and rewrote the
# checked-in file as a side effect of failing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# …except the fonts, named explicitly because they are the files that actually contain CR bytes as
# data and so are the ones an eol rule would corrupt. Anything else binary is caught by `text=auto`.
*.woff2 binary
